## Aim
To identify the top five best-selling products based on total quantity sold using Pandas.

## Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Pandas library.
3. Create a DataFrame containing product names, quantities, and sales dates.
4. Group the data by product name.
5. Calculate the total quantity sold for each product.
6. Sort the quantities in descending order.
7. Display the top five products.
8. Stop the program.

## Code

```python
import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Product": ["Phone", "Laptop", "Phone", "Mouse",
                "Laptop", "Keyboard", "Mouse", "Tablet"],
    "Quantity": [10, 5, 8, 15, 7, 12, 6, 9],
    "Date": ["2026-10-02", "2026-10-05",
             "2026-10-08", "2026-10-10",
             "2026-10-12", "2026-10-15",
             "2026-10-18", "2026-10-20"]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)
df["Date"] = pd.to_datetime(df["Date"])

total_sales = df.groupby("Product")["Quantity"].sum()
top_5 = total_sales.sort_values(
    ascending=False
).head(5)

print("Top 5 Best-Selling Products:")
print(top_5)
```

## Input
Product names, quantities, and dates are provided in the DataFrame.

## Output

```text
Top 5 Best-Selling Products:
Product
Phone       18
Mouse       21
Keyboard    12
Laptop      12
Tablet       9
```

## Result
The products were grouped, ranked according to total quantity sold, and the top five best-selling products were displayed.
